Did you try to join the box with the zero to the box with the covered
nest?

Did you try giving the resulting box to the robot?

Did you think about picking up the 2 and dropping it on the zero?

After you gave the box to the robot did you vacuum away the numbers
in the robot's thought bubble?

Did you give the box back to the robot and wait for him to add up
all the numbers on the nest?

Well, what I would do is drop the box with the nest next to the box
with the zero to join them.  Then I'd give the box to the robot. I'd
train the robot to pick up the 2 and drop it on the zero.  Then I'd
give the box back to the robot and wait for Dusty.  I'd use him to
vacuum up the numbers in the box in the robot's thought bubble.  Then
I'd give the robot the box again and wait for him to finish.  I'd probably
stand up when I got tired of waiting and then sit again.


